From: hnt510 <hnt510@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915: load HuC by default on Gen9-11

Mainline leaves GuC and HuC disabled on every platform before Gen12, so
Skylake through Jasper Lake GPUs boot without HuC.  Their low-power
VDENC encoders need HuC for bitrate control, which VA-API encoders such
as Sunshine and GNOME Remote Desktop use.

Default those platforms to ENABLE_GUC_LOAD_HUC: GuC is loaded only to
authenticate HuC and command submission stays on execlists.  An explicit
i915.enable_guc value still overrides this, Gen12 and newer keep the
upstream defaults, and missing firmware leaves the GPU running without
GuC as before.

Based on the intent of coolsnowwolf/lede x86 992-enable-intel-guc.patch,
which also enabled GuC submission on Gen11; that is not done here.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/gt/uc/intel_uc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/gt/uc/intel_uc.c
@@ -30,12 +30,18 @@
 	if (i915->params.enable_guc != -1)
 		return;
 
-	/* Don't enable GuC/HuC on pre-Gen12 */
-	if (GRAPHICS_VER(i915) < 12) {
+	/* Don't enable GuC/HuC on pre-Gen9 */
+	if (GRAPHICS_VER(i915) < 9) {
 		i915->params.enable_guc = 0;
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/* Load HuC on Gen9-11 for media encoding, keep execlist submission */
+	if (GRAPHICS_VER(i915) < 12) {
+		i915->params.enable_guc = ENABLE_GUC_LOAD_HUC;
+		return;
+	}
+
 	/* Don't enable GuC/HuC on older Gen12 platforms */
 	if (IS_TIGERLAKE(i915) || IS_ROCKETLAKE(i915)) {
 		i915->params.enable_guc = 0;
